      "layering_notes": "Riverside County's Housing and Workforce Solutions (HWS) department runs the Urban County HUD programs, PLHA, HHAP, Homekey+ sponsorships and project loans, while the Housing Authority of the County of Riverside (HACR, same Board sitting as Commissioners) supplies project-based vouchers, housing successor funds and land; rivcohws.org and harivco.org block automated access, so records were built from Board of Supervisors files on riversidecountyca.iqm2.com and media.rivcocob.org, RUHS Behavioral Health, the Assessor and the County Housing Element. PLHA is the County's most flexible recurring source but is spread thin across homebuyer assistance, mobile home parks and $500,000 loans to tax credit deals; it is typically the smallest piece of a stack led by 4% credits, HACR PBVs and a HOME or HOME-ARP loan. Source is the Arroyo Crossing PLHA loan Board file (loan agreement FileOpen ID 85874); allocation figures from the HCD 2024-2028 PLHA NOFA tables.",
